  "body": "Automated bridge job `RQ-SWE2-DOCSLIVING-1` (pool: devin), single commit on base `0b166af3d`.\n\n**Tests:** no test command\n\n<details><summary>Agent notes</summary>\n\n# BRIDGE_NOTES — RQ-SWE2-DOCSLIVING-1\n\n## Summary\n\nLiving-docs sync: one offline engine that regenerates every committed file the\nrepository generates, reports drift as fresh/stale/written/skipped/error, and\nemits a PR-ready proposal (title + body) for the publishing lane. It commits,\npushes and opens nothing — `publish.sh`/sweeps own branch and PR state.\n\nSurfaces (`--surface` selects a subset):\n\n| Surface | File | Source of truth |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `cli` | `docs/cli.md` | `phm --help` + `phm help --all` captures (reuses `generate-cli-docs.mjs`) |\n| `cli-reference` | `docs/CLI-REFERENCE.md` | same captures via `generate-cli-reference.ts` |\n| `llms` | `docs/llms.txt` | generated page-index block (`lib/docs-pages.mjs`) |\n| `codemap` | `docs/CODEMAP.md` | `src/` + `src/core/` directory inventories (new `lib/codemap.mjs`) |\n| `changelog` | `CHANGELOG.md` | `changelog-sync` block inside the live `## [Unreleased]` |\n\nThis extends the `doc-facts.test.ts` parity pattern: the drift guards already\nexisted (`cli-docs-drift`, `cli-reference-drift`, `codemap-drift`,\n`docs-llms-txt`) — this change adds the single writer that satisfies all of\nthem, plus a `syncDocs`-level drift guard for the new engine itself.\n\nSupporting fix: `changelog-sync.mjs update` now tolerates repeated\n`## [Unreleased]` milestone headings (Phantom's CHANGELOG has many) by\nresolving the first/live section; `verify` stays strict — each release tag\nmust still match exactly one section and one non-draft release body. The\n`bridgeSubject` filter now also strips the squash-merge ` (#NNNN)` tail and\ndrops job-id + boilerplate-only subjects, so a git-log-derived snapshot yields\nreader-facing entries only.\n\nThe real `CHANGELOG.md` was deliberately not regenerated in this change: the\nchangelog surface requires explicit scoped evidence (`--changelog-snapshot`\nfrom the GitHub export, or `--changelog-base`); without it the surface reports\n`skipped` rather than guessing history. That one-time adoption is documented\nin `docs/LIVING-DOCS.md` and `scripts/CHANGELOG-SYNC.md`.\n\nDrive-by fix: `docs/README.md`'s `IDLE-ALLOWANCE.md` link is now an absolute\nGitHub URL — the relative link was failing the packaged-links/navigation tests\n(the file is outside the `package.json` `files` allowlist). This was\npre-existing drift from an earlier commit, fixed here because it blocked the\ndocs test lane.\n\n## Files\n\nModified (11):\n\n- `CONTRIBUTING.md` — command-table row for `docs-sync.mjs`\n- `docs/CLI-REFERENCE.md` — regenerated (real drift: missing `metrics idle`,\n  `bus thread|task`, `metrics levers`, updated topic summaries)\n- `docs/CODEMAP.md` — regenerated inventory block\n- `docs/README.md` — LIVING-DOCS index row; IDLE-ALLOWANCE absolute-link fix\n- `docs/cli.md` — regenerated (same underlying help drift)\n- `docs/llms.txt` — regenerated index (adds LIVING-DOCS + previously-missing pages)\n- `scripts/CHANGELOG-SYNC.md` — documents duplicate-heading semantics + markers\n- `scripts/changelog-sync.mjs` — first-section resolution in `sections()`;\n  strict per-tag uniqueness in `verify()`; `bridgeSubject` `(#NNNN)` strip and\n  boilerplate-tail filter\n- `scripts/generate-cli-docs.mjs` — export `SURFACES` for shared capture reuse\n- `scripts/realio-lane-known-fast-spawns.mjs` — add `test/docs-sync.test.ts`\n  (2.2 s slowest test; bounded node/git children, no network)\n- `test/doc-facts.test.ts` — add `docs/LIVING-DOCS.md` to checked docs\n\nNew (5):\n\n- `scripts/lib/living-docs.mjs` — surface registry, plan/write engine,\n  per-surface status + first-difference, proposal builder, changelog snapshot\n  resolution, injected capture seam\n- `scripts/lib/codemap.mjs` — marker-pair codemap block renderer\n- `scripts/docs-sync.mjs` — CLI: `--check|--write`, `--json`, `--root`,\n  `--surface`, `--changelog-snapshot`, `--changelog-base`, `--help`\n  (exit 0 ok / 1 stale-or-error on `--check` / 2 bad usage)\n- `test/docs-sync.test.ts` — 9 tests: fixtures for all five surfaces,\n  plan-no-write, write idempotence, changelog insert/preserve, skipped-without\n  -evidence, generator error, unknown surface, strict verify, real-checkout\n  codemap+llms drift guard\n- `docs/LIVING-DOCS.md` — the guide (usage, surface contract, adoption)\n\nNo `.github/`, CODEOWNERS, workflow or release-config files touched.\n\n## Commands run\n\n| Command | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| `node scripts/verify-changed.mjs --force` | PASS: file selection, fleet-registry skip, `tsc --noEmit`, realio lane (1 pre-existing WARN on unchanged `test/ecosystem-changelog-generator.test.ts`), verse sync-I/O, verify dedupe. SKIP `eslint`: `node_modules/eslint/lib/cli.js` absent locally — Merge Gate runs it in CI. Web typecheck skipped (no `src/web-ui/` change). |\n| `npm run check:docs` | PASS — exit 0, `errors: []`, `externalRequests: 0` |\n| `HOME=$(mktemp -d) npx vitest run` (10 files, 144 tests) | 143 passed; 1 failure: `cli-docs-drift` 5 s test-timeout under 10-way parallel load — passes 6/6 in isolation (below) |\n| `HOME=$(mktemp -d) npx vitest run test/cli-docs-drift.test.ts` | PASS 6/6 in isolation |\n| `HOME=$(mktemp -d) npx vitest run test/docs-sync.test.ts test/doc-facts.test.ts test/docs-readme-links.test.ts` | PASS 69/69 |\n| `node --import tsx scripts/docs-sync.mjs --write` | Regenerated 4 surfaces (cli, cli-reference, llms, codemap); changelog skipped — no scoped evidence |\n| `node --import tsx scripts/docs-sync.mjs --check --json` | PASS — generated surfaces `fresh`; `changelog` `skipped` |\n| `node --import tsx scripts/docs-sync.mjs --help` / bad args / unknown surface | exit 0 / 2 / 2 as specified |\n\nTest totals across affected suites: 144 tests in the combined run (143 pass,\n1 environmental timeout that is green standalone) — every affected file is\ngreen when run at normal parallelism.\n\nFull `npm run lint` could not run: the local ESLint binary is absent from\n`node_modules` (pre-existing environment state). The two lane lints it wraps —\n`lint:realio-lane` and `lint:verse-sync-io` — both ran via `verify-changed`\nand PASS. Full `npm run typecheck` is covered by the passing\n`tsc --noEmit` in `verify-changed`.\n\n## Net LOC\n\n- Tracked diff: **+122 / −73**\n- New untracked files: **+760** (`living-docs.mjs` 251, `docs-sync.test.ts` 232,\n  `docs-sync.mjs` 132, `LIVING-DOCS.md` 90, `codemap.mjs` 55)\n- Total: **+882 / −73 → net +809**\n\n## Boundaries\n\nNo `git commit`, `git push`, tag, `gh pr` mutation or `gh api` write was run;\nevery change is uncommitted in the worktree. Publication stays with\n`publish.sh`/sweeps. The sync engine itself performs only local reads/writes —\nno network, no credentials — and its `proposal` field is the title/body a\npublishing lane can open verbatim.\n</details>\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Added a command to preview, check, or update generated documentation, with reports identifying stale or unavailable pages.\n  * Expanded CLI documentation with additional commands, topics, and observability and integration entries.\n* **Documentation**\n  * Added a guide to keeping living documentation synchronized and updated the documentation index and directory map.\n  * Updated changelog guidance and verification behavior: repeated headings are tolerated during updates, while verification requires exactly one matching section per release tag.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
